"entity": {
"name": "Austevoll Seafood ASA",
"description": "Austevoll Seafood ASA is an pelagic fishery and seafood company, which engages in producing of fish meal and fish oil. It operates through the following segments: LSG, Austral Group, FoodCorp Chile, Br. Birkeland, Kobbevik og Furuholmen Oppdrett, and Pelagia Holding. The LSG segment is involved in fish farming, fishery of white fish and VAP of salmon, trout and white fish, and sale and distribution of fish species and processed fish products. The Austral Group segment includes production of fishmeal, fish oil, canned fish, and frozen fish. The Foodcorp Chile segment holds a fleet of purse-seiner vessels. The Br. Birkeland segment holds pelagic fishing licenses which are utilized by purse-seiner fishing vessels, in addition the company owns vessels with license to fish snow crab. The Kobbevik og Furuholmen Oppdret segment holds salmon farming licenses. The Pelagia Holding segment engages in the production of fishmeal, fish oil, Omega-3 oil, frozen fish for direct human consumption; and protein concentrate and oil based on cuttings from the salmon insustry, whitefish industry, and pelagic cuttings. The company was founded by Helge Arvid Mogster, Ole Rasmus Mogster, and Alf Mogster on April 14, 1981 and is headquartered in Storebo, Norway.",
